course: dictionary
lesson: 1174
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. «Broken» is a good example. Its basic meaning is damaged or in pieces, but the words around it show you which meaning the writer wants.
explain: «The TV is broken» means it is not working. A «broken promise» is one that was not kept. A «broken bone» is a cracked bone. Look at the words next to broken and they will tell you which meaning fits.
explain: Broken is also the past participle of the verb break (break, broke, broken). You will see it after has, have or had, as in «The glass has broken.» Here broken is part of a verb, not a describing word.
explain: When a word has more than one meaning, try each one in the sentence. The meaning that still makes sense is the right one. Palaeontologists wrap big bones in plaster jackets, like a cast on a broken arm, so the bones are safe. Here broken means cracked.
fact: Broken means damaged, or in pieces.
fact: Broken can also mean not working, as in «The TV is broken».
fact: A broken bone is a cracked bone. «A cast is a hard shell of plaster or fibreglass that stops a broken bone moving while it heals.»
fact: «The collarbone often breaks from a fall on the shoulder, and most broken collarbones are treated with a sling, not a cast.»
fact: Broken English is spoken with many mistakes.
exercise: «The TV is broken, so we cannot watch the film.» What does broken mean here? | Full of sadness | Ready to eat | *Not working | Very far away
exercise: Ella says «She made a broken promise.» What does this mean? | A promise made in the rain | Speaking with many mistakes | *A promise that was not kept | A promise written in pencil
exercise: Find and copy the word from «A cast stops a broken bone moving while it heals.» that means cracked or damaged. | cast | heals | moving | *broken
test: «Her arm was broken in the fall, so the doctor put on a cast.» What does broken mean? | Lost in the park | *Cracked or in pieces | Wet from the rain | Happy and laughing
test: Ravi says broken English means speaking very fast. What is the right meaning? | Quiet and gentle | Speaking very fast | *Spoken with many mistakes | Written in a book
exam: Which sentence uses broken to mean not working? | The sandwich was broken in half on the plate | The sky was broken by a bright rainbow | She told a broken joke at the party | *The printer is broken, so we cannot print
